# 5. AI vs Machine Learning vs Deep Learning vs Generative AI

These terms are related but have different meanings.

## 5.1 Artificial Intelligence

AI is the broad field of developing intelligent computer systems.

## 5.2 Machine Learning (ML)

Machine Learning is a subset of AI that allows computers to learn patterns from data without requiring every rule to be explicitly programmed.

Example: Predicting house prices using previous housing data.

## 5.3 Deep Learning (DL)

Deep Learning is a subset of Machine Learning that uses multi-layered artificial neural networks to learn complex patterns.

Example:
- Speech recognition.
- Image recognition.
- Advanced language models.

## 5.4 Generative AI

Generative AI is a category of AI that creates new content based on patterns learned from training data.

It can generate:
- Text.
- Images.
- Audio.
- Video.
- Code.

Examples: ChatGPT, image-generation systems, and AI coding assistants.

### Relationship Diagram

```text
Artificial Intelligence (AI)
          |
          v
   Machine Learning (ML)
          |
          v
    Deep Learning (DL)
          |
          v
   Many Generative AI Systems
```

**Note:** This diagram shows a simplified relationship. Not all generative AI systems use deep learning, and not all deep learning systems are generative.

### Comparison Table

| Feature | AI | ML | Deep Learning | Generative AI |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Meaning | Intelligent systems | Learning from data | Neural-network-based learning | Creating new content |
| Scope | Broadest | Subset of AI | Subset of ML | AI approach/category |
| Main Purpose | Intelligent behavior | Prediction and pattern learning | Complex pattern learning | Content generation |
| Example | Rule-based expert system | Spam classifier | Image recognition model | ChatGPT |

