# 8. Data in Artificial Intelligence

Data is one of the most important elements of AI.

The quality of an AI system depends significantly on the quality and relevance of its data.

## 8.1 Types of Data

### A. Structured Data

Data organized in rows and columns.

Examples:
- Excel spreadsheets.
- SQL databases.
- Customer records.

### B. Unstructured Data

Data that does not follow a fixed tabular structure.

Examples:
- Images.
- Videos.
- Audio recordings.
- Emails.
- Documents.

### C. Semi-Structured Data

Data that has some organization but does not follow a strict relational table structure.

Examples:
- JSON.
- XML.
- HTML.

## 8.2 Training, Validation, and Testing Data

A dataset is commonly divided into three parts.

### Training Data

Used to teach the model and help it learn patterns.

### Validation Data

Used during model development to tune parameters and compare model configurations.

### Testing Data

Used to evaluate the final model on unseen data.

### Example Split

For a dataset containing 1,000 records:

| Dataset | Percentage | Records |
|---|---:|---:|
| Training | 70% | 700 |
| Validation | 15% | 150 |
| Testing | 15% | 150 |

These percentages are examples. Actual splits depend on the problem and dataset size.

## 8.3 Data Quality

Good data should be:

- Accurate.
- Complete.
- Consistent.
- Relevant.
- Up to date.
- Representative.

Poor-quality data can produce inaccurate or biased AI outputs.

