# 10. Introduction to Deep Learning

Deep Learning is a subset of Machine Learning that uses artificial neural networks with multiple layers to learn complex patterns from data.

It is inspired by the structure and functioning of the human brain, although artificial neural networks are simplified mathematical systems.

## 10.1 Why Deep Learning?

Traditional ML often depends on manually designed features.

Deep Learning can learn useful representations directly from large amounts of raw or partially processed data.

Applications:
- Image recognition.
- Speech recognition.
- Language translation.
- Autonomous driving.
- Generative AI.

## 10.2 Traditional ML vs Deep Learning

| Traditional ML | Deep Learning |
|---|---|
| Often needs manual feature engineering | Can automatically learn features |
| Can work with smaller datasets | Often benefits from large datasets |
| Usually less computationally expensive | Often requires more computing power |
| Includes decision trees and regression | Uses multi-layer neural networks |

