# 19. Challenges and Risks of AI

## 19.1 Data Privacy

AI systems may process personal information.

Organizations must protect data and follow applicable privacy laws.

## 19.2 Bias and Fairness

If training data contains unfair patterns, an AI model may reproduce those patterns.

Example: A recruitment model may unfairly rank candidates if its training data reflects historical discrimination.

## 19.3 Explainability

Some complex AI models are difficult to interpret.

It may be challenging to understand why a particular prediction was generated.

## 19.4 Security

AI systems can be exposed to:
- Data poisoning.
- Adversarial attacks.
- Prompt injection.
- Model theft.
- Unauthorized access.

## 19.5 Reliability

AI outputs may be inaccurate, inconsistent, or incomplete.

Important decisions should include suitable verification and human oversight.

